# Link does not follow the name that is joined, so it expects the closure to stay as made and the plan makes it slim; the walk folds the name and calls Object.create() in line.
# JSObject::didBecomePrototype() gives a slim closure that becomes a prototype the storage of its own names (SlimClosure::reify()). No read of the language answers otherwise behind it: length, name and prototype
# were there, with those values and attributes; a slim closure has no storage that emitted code could hold on to, and whoever reads a name off a closure asks the cell's type at each use.
# The net of effects took it for a write of NamedProperties that the row of operationAOTObjectCreate does not name.
# RUN: walk f1 mechanisms=all
# CHECK: NewClosure function=f2 closureForm=Slim
# CHECK: inlineBuiltin=ObjectCreate
# RUN(NET): run-in-shell mechanisms=all testing=CheckEffectsAtRunTime
# NET: object length,name,prototype
# NET-NEXT: exited with 0
